RESOLVED (2026-07-16, 3rd pass — after the friend tested the deployed site):
    - [x] AR opens ".../v" → "Modèle AR introuvable". Root cause: Cloudflare's
      html_handling 307-redirected the WORKER's own env.ASSETS.fetch('/v.html')
      sub-request to /v, and the binding relayed that redirect, stripping the id.
      Fix: the Worker now follows that single redirect and returns 200 (browser
      keeps its URL), and the QR uses /v?id=… (query, no path segment). Verified
      with curl (307→200) + a hardened ar-worker-verify (redirect:manual, asserts
      200 for /v?id and /v/{id}).
    - [x] Sleeve didn't show in the 3D preview. Now projects onto BOTH arm flanks
      in 3D (GarmentModel SleeveDecal, X-axis DecalGeometry) and in AR. Some
      projection warp is inherent on the small curved sleeve; the print files stay
      dimensionally exact.
    - [x] 3D sleeve decal (was "to be implemented") — done (above).
    - [x] Higher-fidelity AR model (the mannequin "looked like shit"). AR now bakes
      the design onto the REAL tee/hoodie mesh (the same GLB as the 3D preview) via
      DecalGeometry — a photoreal draped garment. The procedural mannequin is now
      the custom (ship-your-own) garment fallback only; the AR gender toggle shows
      only for custom.
    - [ ] Real-device QA of native AR (iOS Quick Look USDZ + Android Scene Viewer)
      over HTTPS — can't be tested headlessly; needs a phone on the live site.
    - [ ] OPTIONAL: if you want a person/body WEARING the tee/hoodie in AR (vs the
      realistic "floating garment"), that needs a sourced CC0 body mesh — say the
      word. Best CC0 candidate found: Khronos glTF-Sample-Assets "Corset" dress-form.

